# [DD-13b.W1.1 r46sem finding 10, RULED 2026-08-30] A blank line ENDS a
# `config` body's continuation, exactly as it ends a block scalar's — the
# body IS the indented continuation, a blank line is not indented, so it
# terminates like any other non-indented line. `config dev` therefore
# gets ONLY `flags i`; the `description` line below the blank belongs to
# the FILE, not to `config dev`. Before this fix `parse_prose` (the block
# scalar production `description` also uses in the head) disagreed with
# `parse_config`'s own body-ending rule by treating an INTERIOR blank
# line as part of the value rather than ending it there — this fixture
# exercises the `config` body half of that disagreement; a head-level
# `description |` block scalar with an interior blank line would have
# exercised the other half identically.
config dev
  flags i

description this belongs to the FILE, not to config dev

pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
